The two rectangles are similar. What is the scale factor from the original to the image?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (1.75,0) node[midway,below] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\draw (1.75,0) -- (1.75,1.05);
\draw (1.75,1.05) -- (0,1.05);
\draw (0,1.05) -- (0,0) node[midway,left] {$3\text{ cm}$};
\node at (0.875,1.45) {Original};
\draw (3.1,0) -- (6.6,0) node[midway,below] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\draw (6.6,0) -- (6.6,2.1);
\draw (6.6,2.1) -- (3.1,2.1);
\draw (3.1,2.1) -- (3.1,0) node[midway,left] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\node at (4.85,2.5) {Image};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The two triangles are similar. What is the scale factor from the original to the image, as a fraction in simplest form?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (3.5,0) node[midway,below] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\draw (3.5,0) -- (0,1.75);
\draw (0,1.75) -- (0,0) node[midway,left] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\node at (1.6,2.1) {Original};
\draw (4.9,0) -- (6.3,0) node[midway,below] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\draw (6.3,0) -- (4.9,0.7);
\draw (4.9,0.7) -- (4.9,0) node[midway,left] {$2\text{ cm}$};
\node at (5.6,1.1) {Image};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
